Z||000000||Fearless Freep||11-07-2001||06:38 PM||||Well, with all troubles and the light at the end of the tunnel starting to shine.  I am trying to get the fiero back up and running.  Last thing I remember was:<P>I was sitting at a light...<BR>The fan kicked in<BR>The altimeter voltage dropped<BR>The oil pressure waivered<BR>Fuel Pump no longer energizes.<P>I had replaced the fuel pump about a year before the tragic event.  Could the pump still be the culprit?  I just replaced the oil sensor thinking that might do that trick......no luck....<P>I had heard at one time that a coil or control sensor would keep the fuel pump etc from kicking over.....<P>Your thoughts before I tow it to a mechanic to look at the pump again?||||reg||10
Z||000001||avengador1||11-07-2001||07:34 PM||||Did you check your fuel pump relay? Do you have fuel pressure? Can you hear the fuel pump running when you first turn the key? I think these questions will help us(people on the pff) determine the problem.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-07-2001||07:41 PM||||Before you worry about parts... check all the stuff in the wire service article in my cave.<P>The key items are fan kicked one and voltage dropped.....<P>chack the charging system too.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
